#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:6
msgid "Pokemon Player"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:8
msgid ""
"Play Pokemon games via headless emulation using the `pokemon-agent` "
"package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:10
msgid "When to Use"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:11
msgid "User says \"play pokemon\", \"start pokemon\", \"pokemon game\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:12
msgid "User asks about Pokemon Red, Blue, Yellow, FireRed, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:13
msgid "User wants to watch an AI play Pokemon"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:14
msgid "User references a ROM file (.gb, .gbc, .gba)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:16
msgid "Startup Procedure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:18
msgid "1. First-time setup (clone, venv, install)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:19
msgid ""
"The repo is NousResearch/pokemon-agent on GitHub. Clone it, then set up a"
" Python 3.10+ virtual environment. Use uv (preferred for speed) to create"
" the venv and install the package in editable mode with the pyboy extra. "
"If uv is not available, fall back to python3 -m venv + pip."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:24
msgid ""
"On this machine it is already set up at /home/teknium/pokemon-agent with "
"a venv ready — just cd there and source .venv/bin/activate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:27
msgid ""
"You also need a ROM file. Ask the user for theirs. On this machine one "
"exists at roms/pokemon_red.gb inside that directory. NEVER download or "
"provide ROM files — always ask the user."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:31
msgid "2. Start the game server"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:32
msgid ""
"From inside the pokemon-agent directory with the venv activated, run "
"pokemon-agent serve with --rom pointing to the ROM and --port 9876. Run "
"it in the background with &. To resume from a saved game, add --load-"
"state with the save name. Wait 4 seconds for startup, then verify with "
"GET /health."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:38
msgid "3. Set up live dashboard for user to watch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:39
msgid ""
"Use an SSH reverse tunnel via localhost.run so the user can view the "
"dashboard in their browser. Connect with ssh, forwarding local port 9876 "
"to remote port 80 on nokey@localhost.run. Redirect output to a log file, "
"wait 10 seconds, then grep the log for the .lhr.life URL. Give the user "
"the URL with /dashboard/ appended. The tunnel URL changes each time — "
"give the user the new one if restarted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:46
msgid "Save and Load"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:48
msgid "When to save"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:49
msgid "Every 15-20 turns of gameplay"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:50
msgid "ALWAYS before gym battles, rival encounters, or risky fights"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:51
msgid "Before entering a new town or dungeon"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:52
msgid "Before any action you are unsure about"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:54
msgid "How to save"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:55
msgid ""
"POST /save with a descriptive name. Good examples: before_brock, "
"route1_start, mt_moon_entrance, got_cut"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:58
msgid "How to load"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:59
msgid "POST /load with the save name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:61
msgid "List available saves"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:62
msgid "GET /saves returns all saved states."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:64
msgid "Loading on server startup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:65
msgid ""
"Use --load-state flag when starting the server to auto-load a save. This "
"is faster than loading via the API after startup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:68
msgid "The Gameplay Loop"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:70
msgid "Step 1: OBSERVE — check state AND take a screenshot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:71
msgid ""
"GET /state for position, HP, battle, dialog. GET /screenshot and save to "
"/tmp/pokemon.png, then use vision_analyze. Always do BOTH — RAM state "
"gives numbers, vision gives spatial awareness."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:75
msgid "Step 2: ORIENT"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:76
msgid "Dialog/text on screen → advance it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:77
msgid "In battle → fight or run"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:78
msgid "Party hurt → head to Pokemon Center"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:79
msgid "Near objective → navigate carefully"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:81
msgid "Step 3: DECIDE"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:82
msgid "Priority: dialog > battle > heal > story objective > training > explore"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:84
msgid "Step 4: ACT — move 2-4 steps max, then re-check"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:85
msgid "POST /action with a SHORT action list (2-4 actions, not 10-15)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:87
msgid "Step 5: VERIFY — screenshot after every move sequence"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:88
msgid ""
"Take a screenshot and use vision_analyze to confirm you moved where "
"intended. This is the MOST IMPORTANT step. Without vision you WILL get "
"lost."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:91
msgid "Step 6: RECORD progress to memory with PKM: prefix"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:93
msgid "Step 7: SAVE periodically"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:95
msgid "Action Reference"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:96
msgid "press_a — confirm, talk, select"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:97
msgid "press_b — cancel, close menu"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:98
msgid "press_start — open game menu"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:99
msgid "walk_up/down/left/right — move one tile"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:100
msgid "hold_b_N — hold B for N frames (use for speeding through text)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:101
msgid "wait_60 — wait about 1 second (60 frames)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:102
msgid "a_until_dialog_end — press A repeatedly until dialog clears"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:104
msgid "Critical Tips from Experience"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:106
msgid "USE VISION CONSTANTLY"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:107
msgid "Take a screenshot every 2-4 movement steps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:108
msgid "The RAM state tells you position and HP but NOT what is around you"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:109
msgid "Ledges, fences, signs, building doors, NPCs — only visible via screenshot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:110
msgid "Ask the vision model specific questions: \"what is one tile north of me?\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:111
msgid "When stuck, always screenshot before trying random directions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:113
msgid "Warp Transitions Need Extra Wait Time"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:114
msgid ""
"When walking through a door or stairs, the screen fades to black during "
"the map transition. You MUST wait for it to complete. Add 2-3 wait_60 "
"actions after any door/stair warp. Without waiting, the position reads as"
" stale and you will think you are still in the old map."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:119
msgid "Building Exit Trap"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:120
msgid ""
"When you exit a building, you appear directly IN FRONT of the door. If "
"you walk north, you go right back inside. ALWAYS sidestep first by "
"walking left or right 2 tiles, then proceed in your intended direction."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:124
msgid "Dialog Handling"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:125
msgid ""
"Gen 1 text scrolls slowly letter-by-letter. To speed through dialog, hold"
" B for 120 frames then press A. Repeat as needed. Holding B makes text "
"display at max speed. Then press A to advance to the next line. The "
"a_until_dialog_end action checks the RAM dialog flag, but this flag does "
"not catch ALL text states. If dialog seems stuck, use the manual hold_b +"
" press_a pattern instead and verify via screenshot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:132
msgid "Ledges Are One-Way"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:133
msgid ""
"Ledges (small cliff edges) can only be jumped DOWN (south), never climbed"
" UP (north). If blocked by a ledge going north, you must go left or right"
" to find the gap around it. Use vision to identify which direction the "
"gap is. Ask the vision model explicitly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:138
msgid "Navigation Strategy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:139
msgid "Move 2-4 steps at a time, then screenshot to check position"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:140
msgid "When entering a new area, screenshot immediately to orient"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:141
msgid "Ask the vision model \"which direction to [destination]?\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:142
msgid "If stuck for 3+ attempts, screenshot and re-evaluate completely"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:143
msgid "Do not spam 10-15 movements — you will overshoot or get stuck"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:145
msgid "Running from Wild Battles"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:146
msgid ""
"On the battle menu, RUN is bottom-right. To reach it from the default "
"cursor position (FIGHT, top-left): press down then right to move cursor "
"to RUN, then press A. Wrap with hold_b to speed through text/animations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:150
msgid "Battling (FIGHT)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/pokemon-player_SKILL.md:151
msgid ""
"On the battle menu FIGHT is top-left (default cursor position). Press A "
"to enter move selection, A again to use the first move. Then hold B to "
"speed through attack animations and text."
msgstr ""

